{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall set these words.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even after you go into exile, you shall remain marked by commandments — you set aside tefillin, you made mezuzot, so that they not be unfamiliar to you when you return. And thus it says (Jeremiah 31:21): ״הציבי לך ציונים״. The intention here is to say that even though we perform the commandments outside the Land, and they are bodily obligations to be performed in every place, the Sages of blessed memory have taught us that the essential performance of them is only in the Holy Land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:36.484186518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}